 "scribe_vocals_2": {
  "text": "Motion, motion. Changing position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line. Common to everything in the universe. Motion, motion. We walk, we ride a bicycle, we run. Sleeping, air moves into and out of our lungs. Blood flows in arteries and veins. Carry people, automobiles, and planes. Water flowing, down a dam, leaves falling from trees. Earth rotates once every twenty-four hours, revolves round the sun. Once in a year, the sun, in motion in the Milky Way, Milky Way. Moving within its local group of galaxies. Rectilinear motion. Uniform acceleration. A set of simple equations. Relative nature of motion. Relative velocity. Point objects valid so far as size is much smaller than the distance it moves in a reasonable duration of time. Real life, good number of situations, size neglected without much error. Motion, motion. Change in position of an object with time. Velocity, acceleration along a straight line.",
