 "sarvam_vocals": {
  "text": "Motion. Motion. Changing position of an object with time. Velocity. Acceleration. Along a straight line. Common to everything in the universe. Motion, motion. We walk, we ride a bicycle, we run. Sleeping. Air moves into and out of our lungs. Blood flows in arteries and veins. Carry people, automobiles, and planes. Water flowing. Down a dam, leaks falling from trees. Earth rotates once every 24 hours, revolves around the sun once in a year. The sun in motion in the Milky Way, Milky Way moving within its local group of galaxies, rectilinear motion. Uniform acceleration, a set of simple equations. Relative nature of motion, relative velocity. Point objects valid so far as size is much smaller than the distance it moves in a reasonable duration of time. Real life, good number of situations. Size neglected without much error.\nMotion, motion, change in position of an object with time.\nVelocity, acceleration along a straight line.",
